<%!-- Self-contained landing page: its own header/footer, no phx-click
bindings — plain server-rendered HEEx for a fast first paint. (The
shared user_menu carries a phx-hook attribute; it is inert without a
LiveView.) Session logic stays display-only (#205): the template
branches on @current_user for the chrome (user menu, dashboard CTA) but
the anonymous render is unchanged. The landing
is also mounted at /about — canonical to / — so the marketing page keeps a
permalink once / becomes the dashboard. (#551 retired the menu's About row:
nothing links /about now, the route stays public.)
Copy lives in gettext — the msgid is the source of truth; the wording is
reviewed at merge (#164). Not extracted: standalone proper nouns
(FluxVale, Forgejo, Umami, Kavita) and the hero dashboard mock's
decorative chrome — the address-bar path, the dashboard labels, app
names, hostnames, and statuses stay literal because the mock is
aria-hidden and the sr-only line describes it.
/catalog hrefs can move to ~p now that the route registers (router.ex)
— left literal here pending that slice's cleanup.
The Offset grammar (#277): four-layer offset hero (sunken circle wash, product
panel, float chip, display headline), two equal lanes with the real
catalog preview, full-bleed catalog + pricing bands with a straddling
honesty capsule, load/scroll reveals + hover lifts in landing.css. The
whole content wraps in .landing.contents — display:contents keeps this
layout's flex contract while scoping the landing styles. --%>

<div class="landing contents">
  <Layouts.flash_group flash={@flash} />
  <%!-- #576: the landing renders its own chrome (no Layouts.public), so
  the env-driven analytics tracker rides here too — rendered only when
  an operator configured both env halves. --%>
  <FluxValeWeb.SiteAnalytics.site_analytics />

  <header class="sticky top-0 z-40 border-b border-line bg-canvas/80 backdrop-blur dark:border-line-strong">
    <div class="wrap flex h-14 items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <a href={~p"/"} aria-label="FluxVale" class="flex w-fit items-center gap-2.5">
        <img
          src={~p"/images/mark.svg"}
          width="28"
          height="28"
          alt=""
          aria-hidden="true"
          class="dark:hidden"
        />
        <img
          src={~p"/images/mark-dark.svg"}
          width="28"
          height="28"
          alt=""
          aria-hidden="true"
          class="hidden dark:block"
        />
        <span class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">FluxVale</span>
      </a>
      <nav aria-label={gettext("Primary")}>
        <ul class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <li class="hidden min-[480px]:block">
            <.nav_link href="/catalog">{gettext("Apps")}</.nav_link>
          </li>
          <li class="hidden min-[480px]:block">
            <.nav_link href="/docs">{gettext("Docs")}</.nav_link>
          </li>
          <li class="hidden min-[480px]:block">
            <.nav_link href="/pricing">{gettext("Pricing")}</.nav_link>
          </li>
          <li class="hidden min-[480px]:block">
            <.nav_link href="/blog">{gettext("Blog")}</.nav_link>
          </li>
          <li :if={is_nil(@current_user)}>
            <.button href={~p"/sign-in"} size="sm">
              {gettext("Sign in")} <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            </.button>
          </li>
          <li :if={@current_user}>
            <%!-- #285 T4: handle + PRIMARY address — same contract as
            the app chrome's menu (post-#287 no mirror fallback
            remains; a nil primary is data drift).
            #551: the Admin row rides the same feed the chrome uses. --%>
            <.user_menu
              username={@current_user.username}
              email={@current_user.primary_email}
              platform_admin={ActorIsPlatformAdmin.platform_admin?(@current_user)}
            />
          </li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="flex-1">
    <%!-- Hero: four calm layers — the sunken circle wash (z0, parallax
    slowest), the product panel (z1, offset right+down), the float
    chip (z1.5, below-left of the hero box), the display headline (z2).
    The panel is the product a visitor lands on: an HTML/CSS dashboard
    preview built from dashboard_live.ex, with real catalog apps and
    status pills. It is decorative and aria-hidden; the float chip says
    this is the dashboard you get. The overlap exists only
    >=900px (landing.css). --%>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="hero-grid">
          <div class="hero-circle px-slow" aria-hidden="true"></div>

          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow rise">{gettext("Managed open source apps")}</p>
            <h1 class="display rise d1">
              {gettext("Open source apps, running in minutes.")}
            </h1>
            <p class="hero-sub rise d2">
              {gettext(
                "Pick one from the catalog, deploy it, and FluxVale keeps it running. Or hand it to your agent from Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code, or any MCP client."
              )}
            </p>
            <div class="hero-ctas rise d3">
              <.button :if={is_nil(@current_user)} href={~p"/sign-in"} class="lift">
                {gettext("Get started")}
              </.button>
              <.button :if={@current_user} href={~p"/"} class="lift">
                {gettext("Your dashboard")}
              </.button>
              <.button href="/catalog" variant="ghost" size="lg">
                {gettext("Browse the catalog")}
              </.button>
              <a
                href={if is_nil(@current_user), do: "/docs/agents", else: "/settings/agents"}
                class="arrowlink hero-agent-link"
              >
                {gettext("Have an agent? Set it up")}
                <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="hero-panel rise d2">
            <div class="px-panel">
              <%!-- The panel window: FluxVale's own chrome around an HTML
              dashboard preview. The mock is decorative and theme-aware;
              the sr-only line under the panel describes it. --%>
              <div class="panel" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="panel-bar">
                  <span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
                  <span class="path">fluxvale.com</span>
                  <span>&nbsp;</span>
                </div>
                <div class="mock" data-testid="hero-mock">
                  <div class="mock-head">
                    <div class="mock-heading">
                      <p class="mock-title">Dashboard</p>
                      <p class="mock-sub">Your apps at a glance.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="mock-actions">
                      <span class="mock-wallet"><span class="dot"></span>Wallet</span>
                      <span class="mock-deploy">Deploy app</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <p class="mock-label">Apps</p>
                  <div class="mock-list">
                    <div class="mock-row">
                      <img
                        src={~p"/images/catalog/forgejo/icon.svg"}
                        width="26"
                        height="26"
                        alt=""
                        class="mock-icon"
                      />
                      <div class="mock-app">
                        <p class="mock-name">Forgejo</p>
                        <p class="mock-host">forgejo.fluxvale.app</p>
                      </div>
                      <span class="mock-status is-running">
                        <span class="dot"></span>Running
                      </span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="mock-row">
                      <img
                        src={~p"/images/catalog/umami/icon.png"}
                        width="26"
                        height="26"
                        alt=""
                        class="mock-icon"
                      />
                      <div class="mock-app">
                        <p class="mock-name">Umami</p>
                        <p class="mock-host">umami.fluxvale.app</p>
                      </div>
                      <span class="mock-status is-running">
                        <span class="dot"></span>Running
                      </span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="mock-row">
                      <img
                        src={~p"/images/catalog/kavita/icon.svg"}
                        width="26"
                        height="26"
                        alt=""
                        class="mock-icon"
                      />
                      <div class="mock-app">
                        <p class="mock-name">Kavita</p>
                        <p class="mock-host">kavita.fluxvale.app</p>
                      </div>
                      <span class="mock-status is-sleeping">Sleeping</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <%!-- Outside .px-panel on purpose: its parallax transform
            would trap the chip on the panel (see landing.css). The
            sr-only line gives the aria-hidden mock a spoken equivalent:
            it is a preview of that dashboard, not a screenshot. --%>
            <div class="float-chip drop d5">
              <span class="dot"></span>{gettext("The dashboard you get")}
              <span class="sr-only">
                {gettext(
                  "A preview of the dashboard with several apps running, not a screenshot."
                )}
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <%!-- How it works: two equal lanes, human first. The human lane
    carries the real catalog preview; the agent lane carries the same
    three steps and its setup link. --%>
    <section aria-labelledby="how-it-works-title" class="steps">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="band-head">
          <p class="eyebrow reveal">{gettext("How it works")}</p>
          <h2 id="how-it-works-title" class="display-h2 reveal">
            {gettext("Two ways to a running app")}
          </h2>
          <p class="band-sub">
            {gettext(
              "Pick an app yourself, or hand it to your agent. FluxVale runs it either way."
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="lanes">
          <div class="lane lane-human reveal">
            <p class="lane-label">{gettext("From the dashboard")}</p>
            <ol class="lane-steps">
              <li class="lane-step">
                <span class="n">01</span>
                <h3>{gettext("Pick an app")}</h3>
                <p>
                  {gettext(
                    "Choose from a curated catalog of open source applications, ready to run."
                  )}
                </p>
              </li>
              <li class="lane-step">
                <span class="n">02</span>
                <h3>{gettext("Deploy")}</h3>
                <p>
                  {gettext(
                    "One guided flow from app to live URL. No YAML, no servers to babysit."
                  )}
                </p>
              </li>
              <li class="lane-step">
                <span class="n">03</span>
                <h3>{gettext("FluxVale runs it")}</h3>
                <p>
                  {gettext("Updates and monitoring are on us. Your data stays yours.")}
                </p>
              </li>
            </ol>
            <div class="mini">
              <span class="cat">{gettext("Developer Tools")}</span>
              <div class="m">
                <span class="chip">FJ</span>
                <span>
                  <b>Forgejo</b>
                  <span class="d">{gettext("Git forge with issues, pull requests, and Actions CI")}</span>
                </span>
              </div>
              <span class="cat">{gettext("Media & Entertainment")}</span>
              <div class="m">
                <span class="chip">KV</span>
                <span>
                  <b>Kavita</b>
                  <span class="d">{gettext("Digital library for comics, manga, and ebooks")}</span>
                </span>
              </div>
              <div class="foot">
                <span class="more">{gettext("…and more in the catalog")}</span>
                <a href="/catalog" class="arrowlink">
                  {gettext("See the catalog")}
                  <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="lane lane-agent reveal">
            <p class="lane-label">{gettext("From your agent")}</p>
            <ol class="lane-steps">
              <li class="lane-step">
                <span class="n">01</span>
                <h3>{gettext("Ask for the app")}</h3>
                <p>
                  {gettext("Tell your agent what you need. It picks the app from the catalog.")}
                </p>
              </li>
              <li class="lane-step">
                <span class="n">02</span>
                <h3>{gettext("The agent deploys")}</h3>
                <p>
                  {gettext("It deploys the app and hands you the URL.")}
                </p>
              </li>
              <li class="lane-step">
                <span class="n">03</span>
                <h3>{gettext("FluxVale runs it")}</h3>
                <p>
                  {gettext("Same platform. Same updates, backups, and private access.")}
                </p>
              </li>
            </ol>
            <div class="lane-foot">
              <span class="clients">
                {gettext("Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code, or any MCP client.")}
              </span>
              <a
                href={if is_nil(@current_user), do: "/docs/agents", else: "/settings/agents"}
                class="arrowlink"
              >
                {gettext("Set up your agent")}
                <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%!-- Ways in: the dashboard is the human path, the agent is its
        peer, and Terraform plus the CLI are the code path. --%>
        <div id="ways" class="ways reveal">
          <div class="ways-head">
            <p class="eyebrow">{gettext("Ways in")}</p>
            <p class="ways-lead">
              {gettext(
                "Use the dashboard, or hand it to your agent. Terraform and the CLI are there for code."
              )}
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="ways-pair">
            <a
              href={if is_nil(@current_user), do: "/sign-in", else: "/"}
              class="way way-dashboard"
              data-testid="way-dashboard"
            >
              <span class="cat">{gettext("For you")}</span>
              <span class="way-title">{gettext("Dashboard")}</span>
              <span class="way-body">
                {gettext(
                  "Pick an app, deploy it, and manage it from the panel. The wallet, backups, and access live there too."
                )}
              </span>
              <span class="arrowlink">
                {if is_nil(@current_user),
                  do: gettext("Get started"),
                  else: gettext("Open the dashboard")}
                <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
              </span>
            </a>
            <a
              href={if is_nil(@current_user), do: "/docs/agents", else: "/settings/agents"}
              class="way way-agent"
              data-testid="way-mcp"
            >
              <span class="cat">{gettext("For your agent")}</span>
              <span class="way-title">{gettext("MCP server")}</span>
              <span class="way-body">
                {gettext(
                  "Point Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code, or any MCP client at FluxVale. OAuth clients connect with the URL and one approval. Clients without OAuth use a scoped token."
                )}
              </span>
              <code class="way-url">https://mcp.fluxvale.com/mcp</code>
              <span class="arrowlink">
                {gettext("Set up your agent")}
                <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
              </span>
            </a>
          </div>
          <div class="ways-code">
            <a href="/docs/automation/terraform" class="way way-code" data-testid="way-terraform">
              <span class="way-title">{gettext("Terraform provider")}</span>
              <span class="way-body">
                {gettext(
                  "Instances, backups, gateways, and custom domains as resources. The provider is on the Terraform and OpenTofu registries."
                )}
              </span>
              <span class="arrowlink">
                {gettext("Provider guide")} <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
              </span>
            </a>
            <a href="/docs/automation/cli" class="way way-code" data-testid="way-cli">
              <span class="way-title">{gettext("FluxVale CLI")}</span>
              <span class="way-body">
                {gettext(
                  "One self-contained binary. Deploy, back up, check the wallet from the terminal."
                )}
              </span>
              <span class="arrowlink">
                {gettext("CLI guide")} <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
              </span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <%!-- App catalog band: full-bleed panel-raised seam; the second
    card rides offset-down at >=900px. --%>
    <section aria-labelledby="catalog-title" class="catalog-band">
      <div class="wrap catalog-in">
        <div class="band-head reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">{gettext("App catalog")}</p>
          <h2 id="catalog-title" class="display-h2">
            {gettext("Pick an app. It's running in minutes.")}
          </h2>
          <p class="band-sub">
            {gettext(
              "Every app is ready to deploy. Browse the catalog yourself, or let your agent pick."
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="catalog-cards">
          <div class="app-card reveal">
            <p class="cat">{gettext("Developer Tools")}</p>
            <div class="app">
              <span class="chip">FJ</span>
              <b>Forgejo</b>
            </div>
            <p>{gettext("Git forge with issues, pull requests, and Actions CI")}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="app-card offset-down reveal">
            <p class="cat">{gettext("Media & Entertainment")}</p>
            <div class="app">
              <span class="chip">KV</span>
              <b>Kavita</b>
            </div>
            <p>{gettext("Digital library for comics, manga, and ebooks")}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="catalog-cta reveal">
          <a href="/catalog" class="arrowlink">
            {gettext("Browse the catalog")} <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <%!-- Pricing: sunken band; the honesty capsule straddles the seam
    (#277 pattern). --%>
    <section aria-labelledby="pricing-title" class="pricing-band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="capsule-slot drop d5">
          <span class="capsule">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            {gettext(
              "Every app runs on infrastructure we manage for you. Updates, TLS, backups, and monitoring are included."
            )}
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="pricing-in">
          <div>
            <h2 id="pricing-title" class="reveal">
              {gettext("One flat rate, no surprises")}
            </h2>
            <%!-- #396 + #558: the band points at /pricing now — the
            sub-copy is resource-framed and semicolon-free. The floor
            line renders the cheapest compute class's rate with storage
            named as its own per-GB charge (hidden on an unseeded
            table; the controller passes nil then). --%>
            <p class="sub reveal">
              {gettext(
                "Prices follow the resources an app gets, not the app itself. Your agent can check the price before it deploys. New accounts start with a welcome credit. Top up when you're ready."
              )}
            </p>
            <p :if={not is_nil(@price_floor_cents)} class="sub reveal">
              <%!-- pricing.ex's #206 invariant: a price surface never
              shows "$X/mo" without the hourly qualifier — a bare "/mo"
              on the landing would read as monthly billing. --%>
              {gettext(
                "Compute starts at %{rate}/mo plus per-GB storage, billed hourly while running",
                rate: FluxVale.Pricing.format_usd(@price_floor_cents)
              )}
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="pricing-side reveal">
            <span class="eyebrow">{gettext("Simple pricing")}</span>
            <.button href="/pricing" class="lift">
              {gettext("See full pricing")}
            </.button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <%!-- #881: the ONE public footer — the same public_footer/1 the
  public chrome renders, defined once in layouts.ex. The landing's
  own frame keeps its header; the footer is shared. --%>
  <Layouts.public_footer current_user={@current_user} return_to={@return_to} />
</div>
